  "findings": [
    "Lift-cache keys still include complete path, digest, original depth and requested depth. The eight-way bucket is only a lookup hint; hits compare all fields. Borrow contention retains the original uncached calculation. The fixed table changes replacement policy without storing an authorization, SQL, graph, ancestry, or commit verdict.",
    "The 8192-entry slot array is lazy and bounded; the compile-time software charge is for this table and its RefCell, not process RSS or the separate node-decode cache. The deterministic replacement state is explicitly not a security random source.",
    "The actual original 44d module executed six successful cases and left two diagnostics ignored on x86_64 and aarch64. These observations are not a new composed-head run or a Host/business performance qualification.",
    "Cold witness open requires the caller's expected authenticated Checkpoint and then reads the actual durable head. The revised expiry path keeps the no-expiry IMMEDIATE transaction and performs the original fresh mutation guard after a real expiry commit. The cold-recovery tests and required selector inventory remain in the frozen owner tree.",
    "Linux x86_64/aarch64 sha2 asm selection and known-answer tests are adopted intact. The separate fuzz lock is generated by actual Cargo and bound to that same owner manifest."
  ],
